  "limitations": [
    "Verus proves actual generic frontier operations, unique pending identities and seen preservation under ENV-STRING-KEY. Surrounding loops, JSON identity/edge decoding, file I/O, allocation and whole-API conformance remain unproved.",
    "The finite TLA model explores all directed graphs/cache subsets on three nodes. Complete immutable expansion/cache values are ENV-GRAPH assumptions; real byte-level failures and composition with Ownership are outside this model.",
    "Valid local references still precede their parent manifest. Cycles in the abstract model are defensive exploration, not a claim that authenticated cyclic manifests can be constructed.",
    "Heap-backed traversal removes one native call frame per dependency level. Graph/index/cache memory still grows; many explicitly cached roots can still consume large memory. No arbitrary JSON nesting or memory bound is proved.",
    "Measurements use one leaf pack and one inline-manifest chain pack per pool, ascending levels, warm repeated validations and four concurrent clients. Load/cache state is uncontrolled and p99 is not a hard bound.",
    "First-root-retain has four observations per level after validation and with leaf/raw-reference closure caches; it is not a cold-cache or retain-p99 measurement.",
    "This is control-path latency, not payload bandwidth. The prior 100 GB run and sparse TB-offset checks were not rerun or relabeled for this change."
  ],
